  "trigger_name": "Voluntary / Third-Party Report",
  "summary_html": "Any person may submit a **third-party report** to child-protection authorities. In North Carolina such a report is not optional: any person or institution with cause to suspect abuse, neglect, or dependency must report to the county director of social services (N.C. Gen. Stat. § 7B-301(a)). CAPTA requires states to maintain mechanisms for intake, confidentiality, and immunity policies tied to federal funding.",
  "authority_html": "- **CAPTA (42 U.S.C. §§ 5101–5116)** — requires states to operate intake/report systems that accept voluntary reports and protect good-faith reporters",
