          "case_name": "Dobson v. Harris",
          "citation": "352 N.C. 77, 530 S.E.2d 829 (2000)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of North Carolina",
          "year": 2000,
          "date_decided": "2000-06-16",
          "holding": "The Supreme Court held that the statutory presumption of good faith for persons reporting suspected child abuse or neglect shifts to the plaintiff the burden of producing factual (not speculative) evidence of bad faith or malice, and that summary judgment for the reporter is proper absent such a forecast.",
          "relevance": "It sets the evidentiary burden a subject of a voluntary third-party report must meet to sue the reporter.",
          "quote": "Evidence offered to meet or rebut the presumption of good faith must be sufficient by virtue of its reasonableness, not by mere supposition.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1203470/dobson-v-harris/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1203470
        },
        {
          "case_name": "In re Stumbo",
          "citation": "357 N.C. 279, 582 S.E.2d 255 (2003)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of North Carolina",
          "year": 2003,
          "date_decided": "2003-07-16",
          "holding": "The Supreme Court held that a single anonymous report that a two-year-old was seen naked and unsupervised in her own driveway did not describe neglect under N.C.G.S. § 7B-101 and therefore never triggered the mandatory investigation power of § 7B-302, so the § 7B-303 non-interference order against the parents had to be reversed.",
          "relevance": "It holds that a third-party report must actually allege facts amounting to abuse, neglect, or dependency before DSS acquires its statutory investigative powers.",
          "quote": "a single report of a naked, unsupervised two-year-old in the driveway of her home does not trigger the investigative requirements of N.C.G.S. § 7B-302",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1285049/in-re-stumbo/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1285049
        }
